= Token (blockchain) =

== Overview ==
'''Token (blockchain)''' is a ledger-managed representation of an asset, unit, claim, access right, or other transferable or account-associated state defined by a blockchain protocol or smart contract.

Tokens can be fungible or non-fungible, transferable or restricted, native to a ledger or implemented through smart-contract standards. Their semantics come from the protocol, code, issuer, governance, and surrounding legal or social context.

A token record can represent a claim on something outside the blockchain, but the ledger cannot by itself guarantee that the external asset exists, remains redeemable, or has the represented legal status.

Not every blockchain token is a cryptocurrency, and the word 'token' is heavily overloaded in authentication, natural-language processing, software, and economics.

== Boundaries ==
* blockchain token ≠ cryptocurrency by definition
* token record ≠ external asset itself
* token ≠ authentication token / language token

